  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_audit_retention_days" version_id="1026300" version_string="1.2.63"><![CDATA[How many days of AI action-log entries to keep. A daily cron prunes older rows. 0 = never prune (keep everything).]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_nav_bottom" version_id="1011600" version_string="1.1.16"><![CDATA[Adds an AI Connect icon button next to the RSS feed link in the page footer.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_nav_top" version_id="1022500" version_string="1.2.25"><![CDATA[<strong>Master switch</strong> for guest visibility. When disabled, guests cannot see the AI Connect navigation link or access the info page — regardless of the <em>viewAiConnect</em> permission.<br><br>When enabled, guest access is controlled by the <em>viewAiConnect</em> permission (Admin CP → User Groups → Permissions → AI Connect).<br><br>Logged-in users with <em>useTools</em> permission always see the link and can access the page, regardless of this setting.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_rate_limit_per_hour" version_id="1025900" version_string="1.2.59"><![CDATA[Maximum tool calls allowed per hour per token/identifier. Default 1000.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_rate_limit_per_minute" version_id="1025900" version_string="1.2.59"><![CDATA[Maximum tool calls allowed per minute per token/identifier. Default 50. Set 0 for the built-in default.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_rate_limit_read_per_minute" version_id="1026100" version_string="1.2.61"><![CDATA[Optional separate cap on read/GET tool calls per minute per user. 0 = disabled (only the global per-minute/per-hour limits apply). Use this to allow generous reads while keeping writes conservative.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_rate_limit_write_per_minute" version_id="1026100" version_string="1.2.61"><![CDATA[Optional separate cap on write/POST tool calls per minute per user. 0 = disabled. Set a low value (e.g. 10) to throttle AI posting while leaving reads generous.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_require_bearer_header" version_id="1025900" version_string="1.2.59"><![CDATA[When ON, the tools endpoint refuses the ?token= query-string fallback and accepts only the Authorization: Bearer header. Recommended: a live token in a URL leaks into browser history, proxy logs and web-server access logs. OFF by default so existing GET ?token= integrations keep working.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.aiconnect_translation_provider" version_id="1012900" version_string="1.1.29"><![CDATA[Choose how translation works for AI agents connected to your forum.<br><br><b>AI Self-Translate</b> — The AI agent translates content using its own language abilities. No external API, no limits, best quality. <em>Recommended.</em><br><b>MyMemory API</b> — Uses the free <a href="https://mymemory.translated.net/" target="_blank">MyMemory</a> translation service. Limited to ~5,000 characters/day.<br><b>Disabled</b> — No translation capability offered to AI agents.]]></phrase>
